    "md5": "b5017426d13a208a4e8c92b15be91c60",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1983,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka new govt establishes ministerial investigation units amid criticism\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 Sri Lanka\u2019s new government has decided to establish investigation units in each ministry to hold public officials accountable amid large number of complaints against those officials and criticism of trade unions dictating terms in ministries.\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake-led ruling National People\u2019s Power (NPP) has promised an overhaul in the governance to ensure accountability and transparency while eliminating corruption.\n\nTens of thousands of Sri Lankans demanded a system change in the governance to hold rulers accountable for their actions during 2022 mass protests which led to oust then President Gotabaya Rajapaksa and his government which declared bankruptcy in April that year.\n\nHowever, top NPP officials have said the \u201csystem change\u201d is not as easy as they had thought earlier, given public officials have been doing the same thing what they are used to, including long delays in the discharging their duties in the public service.\n\n\u201cAt present, a large number of complaints pertaining to public service are being received daily, nominally and anonymously, by the president\u2019s office, the prime minister\u2019s office, as well as public representatives,\u201d the government said in its official cabinet decisions document.\n\n\u201cIn order to protect the public trust kept in the government, and especially in order to make prospective positive changes in the public service, an impartial and scientific investigation of such complaints should be carried out.\u201d\n\n\u201cAccordingly, the Cabinet of Ministers has approved the proposal presented by his Excellency, the President, to establish investigation units\u2026. to investigate the facts pertaining to the functioning of public institutions under the previous government, public complaints, statements, and information reported from various sources regarding the functioning of the current public institutions.\u201d"
  },
