    "description": "Sri Lanka new govt establishes ministerial investigation units amid criticism",
    "url_metadata": "https://economynext.com/sri-lanka-new-govt-establishes-ministerial-investigation-units-amid-criticism-197334/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "economynextcom",
    "time_ut": 1735653600.0,
    "chunk_id": "2024-12-31-economynextcom-77a9e2cc-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a95707d2ac339f34397e6d7636081405",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1105,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cAccordingly, the Cabinet of Ministers has approved the proposal presented by his Excellency, the President, to establish investigation units\u2026. to investigate the facts pertaining to the functioning of public institutions under the previous government, public complaints, statements, and information reported from various sources regarding the functioning of the current public institutions.\u201d\n\nThe move also comes amid increasing criticism of public officials with lower grade who are attached to Marxists Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP) trade unions trying to dictate terms in their respective public offices and complaining about their seniors.\n\nThe JVP is the largest coalition partner of the NPP and it has strong trade unions across the country.\n\nSome public officials who are holding executive grades have said their decisions are being scrutinized by the lower officials because of the affiliation with NPP trade unions.\n\nSri Lanka has not implemented strong accountability measures in public offices except for some politically-motivated witch hunting in the past. (Colombo/December 31/2024)"
