    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-01-01-adaderanalk-cd82034a",
    "num": "adaderanalk-cd82034a",
    "date_str": "2025-01-01",
    "description": "Heavy showers expected in parts of the island",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.adaderana.lk/news/104632/heavy-showers-expected-in-parts-of-the-island",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "adaderanalk",
    "time_ut": 1735700160.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-01-01-adaderanalk-cd82034a-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "07c4c11e7be50a789b16a338a3ccf55a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1144,
    "chunk_text": "Heavy showers expected in parts of the island\n\nThe Meteorology Department says showers or thundershowers will occur at times in Eastern and Uva provinces and in Matale, Nuwara-Eliya, Polonnaruwa, Hambantota and Matara districts.\n\nHeavy showers above 100 mm can be expected at some places in Eastern and Uva provinces and in Matale, Nuwara-Eliya and Hambantota districts.\n\nSeveral spells of showers may occur in the Northern provinceand in Anuradhapura district, the Met. Department said.\n\nShowers or thundershowers will occur at several places elsewhere during the afternoon or night.\n\nFairly heavy showers above 75 mm can be expected at some places in Western, Sabaragamuwa provinces and in Galle district.\n\nFairly strong winds of 30-40 kmph can be expected at times over Northern, Eastern, North-central, North-western and Southern provinces,it added.\n\nMisty conditions can be expected at some places in Western, Sabaragamuwa and Central provinces during the morning.\n\nThus, the general public is kindly requested to take adequate precautions to minimize damages caused by temporary localized strong winds and lightning during thundershowers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
