    "md5": "f33bfb835fc09d9baa0ea0afd2c1aeed",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1282,
    "chunk_text": "Leaders are groomed from school days; many corporate organisations of yesteryear gave preference to people with proven leadership achievements during their school careers when recruiting school leavers for their companies. These organisations had the benefit of absorbing well-groomed leaders during their tender age.\n\nIn Sri Lanka, individual performances take precedence over the team performance. These individual performances should be rewarded then and there like rewarding the best batsman, man of the match and best bowler at a cricket encounter. etc. The mistake people always make is, just because someone gives a brilliant performance, he is considered for a promotion rather than checking whether he has the potential to perform by leading his team at a different level. People tend to forget that it is the team performance that matters than individual brilliance, when considering a person for a leadership role. The other mistake that people often make is thinking that the good performer cannot be replaced - he/she is so good that no equal replacement can be found. If this is true, the world would not have developed to this extent. No one is indispensable, better performers will emerge. Records are not static, they are there to be broken and they will be broken."
