    "md5": "6b40391feebbd3feee1c854463484af4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1120,
    "chunk_text": "Right of Response to Caritas Sri Lanka\n\nWe refer to the published studies by Caritas Sri Lanka titled Research Study on the Culture and Identity of the Plantation Community in Sri Lanka\u00a0and Right to Education of the Children of the Plantation Community.\n\nAt the outset, we express our appreciation to the Catholic Bishops Conference and Caritas Sri Lanka for their interest and recommendations aimed at creating an enabling environment for preserving and promoting the culture and identity of plantation communities. We recognize that the recommendations in these publications encompass a wide range of areas, including inclusive development policies, education and awareness programs, cultural preservation funding, legal protection, economic empowerment, and the promotion of culture-based tourism. While we respect the commitment of Caritas to these communities, we believe the data used in their reports should be revisited to reflect today\u2019s on-the-ground realities. Our goal is to offer updated information so that all stakeholders can align on how best to support plantation communities most effectively today."
  },
