    "chunk_text": "\u201cMy father had not been well about a year-and-a-half before due to a urinary infection which he neglected and as a result the toxin backtracked into his blood stream. It took him two months of hospital treatment to get back to normalcy. Age surely had caught up with him but he was a healthy 89. He was not eating much and that had made him weak. On that fateful day he was reclining in his bed with my mother seated near his feet and had some tea.\n\nThis article written for the \u201cSpotlight\u201d Column appears in the \u201cDaily FT\u201d of November 28, 2015. It can be accessed here: http://www.ft.lk/d-b-s-jeyaraj"
