    "chunk_size_bytes": 801,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Trump tariff shock too early to assess: CB Governor\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 The shock to Sri Lanka from a Trump tariff is too early to assess, Central Bank Governor Nandalal Weerasinghe said, though slower global due from the fallout has been factored in to macro-economic projections.\n\n\u201cWhat we do not know is if there is a shock to the economy,\u201d Governor Weerasinghe said earlier this week.\n\nIt was too early to predict whether there would be employment losses, he said.\n\nSri Lanka has reduced its 44 percent Trump tariff to 30 percent is negotiating to bring it down further to ensure that competing countries do not have lower rates.\n\nThe International Monetary Fund has said gross domestic product could be hit between 0.25-1.5 percent depending on what the rate was. (Colombo/July13/2025)"
  },
