    "md5": "f4afd8fa336f57be7ce109b4d5549ff1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1688,
    "chunk_text": "India-funded 115-unit housing project opens in Anuradhapura\n\nPrime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya and Indian High Commissioner Santosh Jha last Saturday jointly inaugurated and handed over to the beneficiaries houses constructed with Indian assistance under the Sri Sobitha Nahimigama Project in the Anuradhapura district.\n\nThe project envisaged the construction of 115 houses and other infrastructure facilities for residents of the Elapathgama village in Anuradhapura. It was undertaken based on a request by the Ven. Maduluwawe Sobitha Thero Commemoration Foundation, in line with the vision of the Late Venerable Thero for the development of the poverty-stricken village located in the dry zone of the North Central Province. The village with the new facilities would be renamed Sri Sobitha Nahimigama.\n\nIn his remarks, High Commissioner Jha underscored the shared commitment of the Governments of India and Sri Lanka to the welfare of the people of the two countries, and the synergy in approaches in this regard \u2013 with India marching towards \u2018Viksit Bharat\u2019 with the motto of \u2018Sabka Saath, Sabka Vikas,\u2019 and Sri Lanka having embarked on a path towards \u2018A Thriving Nation and a Beautiful Life.\u2019\n\nRecalling the numerous development cooperation initiatives of India in Anuradhapura, such as the recently launched India-assisted signalling system for the Maho-Anuradhapura railway line and the upgraded Maho-Omanthai railway track, as well as committed ones, such as the development of the Sacred City Complex, the High Commissioner reiterated India\u2019s commitment to continue working with Sri Lanka across all dimensions of the bilateral relationship for mutual benefit."
  },
