    "chunk_text": "Recalling the numerous development cooperation initiatives of India in Anuradhapura, such as the recently launched India-assisted signalling system for the Maho-Anuradhapura railway line and the upgraded Maho-Omanthai railway track, as well as committed ones, such as the development of the Sacred City Complex, the High Commissioner reiterated India\u2019s commitment to continue working with Sri Lanka across all dimensions of the bilateral relationship for mutual benefit.\n\nA Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was accordingly signed between the Government of India and the Urban Development and Housing Ministry of Sri Lanka in July 2017. Under the revised contours of the project, the Government of India increased its financial assistance commitment to over Rs. 450 million for 90 houses, while the Government of Sri Lanka built 25 houses and other facilities, such as a residence for monks and a library. The latter were inaugurated and handed over at a ceremony held earlier in April 2024. With the handing over of the 90 houses on Saturday, the project now stands fully completed.\n\nUrban Development, Construction and Housing Minister. Anura Karunathilaka, Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Minister Wasantha Samarasinghe, Urban Development, Construction and Housing Deputy Minister T.B. Sarath, former Speaker of Parliament Karu Jayasuriya, Anuradhapura District Secretary MP Prof. Sena Nanayakkara, Sobitha Thero Foundation President Ravi Jayawardana, among other dignitaries, also attended the event."
