    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka rupee weaker, bond yields flat\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 Sri Lanka\u2019s rupee closed at 301.00/15 to the US dollar in the spot market Tuesday, slightly weaker from 300.97/301.00 a day earlier, while bond yields were flat.\n\nThe market awaited news on Trump tariffs, with opinion on the reduced 30 percent rate divided. But fiscal performance was improving.\n\nIn the secondary market, a bond maturing 15.12.2026 was closed at 8.05/15 percent, flat from 8.05/15 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.09.2027 close at 8.45/55 percent, flat.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.03.2028 closed at 8.75/85 percent from 8.75/80 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2029 closed at 9.48/52 marginally up from 9.48/54 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 01.06.2033 was closed 10.70/90 percent, stead from 10.70/73 percent. (Colombo/Jul15/2025)"
