    "md5": "e836431f73dc0e3fda3e5c4e2880c4cd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1882,
    "chunk_text": "Biggest crossing by a company on a particular day; turnover hits Rs 17 billion\n\nCSE activities were dominated by HNB yesterday, because out of 53.1 percent (Non- Voting) shares held by Browns Investments, 38.5 million shares were sold to 207 investors by way of an arranged transaction or crossing, thus registering the biggest crossing made by a single company in a day, market analysts said.\n\nBrowns Investments sold below the previous day\u2019s market price of Rs 280, resulting in the market coming down despite the whopping turnover of Rs 17 billion, enabling the market to perform in a downward trend.\n\nThe All Share Price Index went down by 61.3 points while S and P SL20 declined by 43.45 points. Turnover stood at Rs 17 billion with six crossings.\n\nThose crossings were reported in HNB (Non- Voting) 38.5 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 10 billion; its shares traded at Rs 280, HNB (Voting) 1.95 million share volumes crossed for Rs 702 million and its shares traded at Rs 360, JKH 8.9 million shares crossed for Rs 230 million; its shares traded at Rs 25.60, Access Engineering 1.9 million share volumes crossed to the tune of Rs 110 million and its shares traded at Rs 58, Distilleries 990,000 shares crossed for Rs 44.6 million; its shares sold at Rs 45 and Lanka IOC 185,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 24.2 million; its shares traded at Rs 131.\n\nIn the retail market, the top companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; HNB (Voting) Rs 515 million (1.4 million shares traded), Sampath Bank Rs 327 million (2.3 million shares traded), JKH Rs 308 million (12 million shares traded), Browns Investments Rs 274 million (35 million shares traded), Access Engineering Rs 243 million (4.2 million shares traded) and HNB (Non- Voting) Rs 232 million (804,000 shares traded). During the day 301 million share volumes changed hands in 38172 transactions."
